 ## Background
-The specific loss formulations described here originate from various recent advances in differentiable rendering and neural scene representation. The standard photometric loss (Final Loss Function) is foundational to the original NeRF paper [S1]. The Multi-scale Voxel Color Loss was introduced in FrugalNeRF to address convergence speed and detail preservation in few-shot settings [S1]. The Rate-Distortion Optimization Loss addresses the need for compact representations in volumetric video coding [S2]. The GO-NeRF optimization strategy, including its specific loss weighting and background augmentation, was developed for virtual reality content creation [S2]. StegaNeRF introduced the classifier loss for embedding invisible information [S3]. StyleNeRF adapted GAN-based objectives with NeRF path regularization for high-resolution synthesis [S4, unofficial].
